  "details": "Udon is good. It offers a lot of customization. Ive toyed with it myself. \n\nHowever, it is unreasonable to expect someone to know udon for basic things, like toggling an object, or a basic teleport. Community made things like cyantrigger bridged that gap, and used udon to create a sort of trigger shell. \n\nWhy cant vrchat just have that itself? this game was built on random people with no unity experience just playing around. Allow some of that simplicity and ease of access provided by triggers, to coexist with Udon. Cyan Trigger already proves that works. But that addon is no longer supported. And vrc shouldnt have to rely on something like that, for ease of access.\n\nagain, not saying kill udon or udon bad, Just that maybe you should consider not catering only to people who can code, and include a few out of the box things like you used to.",
